         ← ChannelPort concept + OutboundChannelPorts\n│   ├── embedding.nim                    ← EmbeddingPort concept\n│   ├── http.nim                         ← HttpPort concept\n│   ├── ipc.nim\n│   ├── memory.nim                       ← MemoryPort concept\n│   ├── provider.nim                     ← ProviderPort concept\n│   ├── secrets.nim                      ← SecretStore concept\n│   └── tool.nim                         ← ToolPort concept\n└── tui/\n    └── dashboard.nim\n```\n\n## Full Directory Tree: tests/\n\n```\ntests/\n├── adapters/\n│   ├── channel/\n│   │   ├── t_common_runtime.nim\n│   │   ├── t_qq_onebot.nim\n│   │   ├── t_qq_runtime.nim\n│   │   ├── t_telegram_runtime.nim\n│   │   └── t_wechat.nim\n│   └── network/\n│       └── t_dns_resolver.nim\n├── app/\n│   ├── t_agent_runner.nim\n│   ├── t_daemon_ingress.nim\n│   ├── t_doctor.nim\n│   ├── t_heartbeat.nim\n│   ├── t_http_gateway.nim\n│   ├── t_native_tools.nim\n│   ├── t_orchestrator.nim\n│   ├── t_outbound_runtime.nim\n│   ├── t_sandbox.nim\n│   ├── t_session_bootstrap.nim\n│   └── t_session_manager.nim\n├── architecture/\n│   └── t_boundaries.nim\n├── channel/\n│   ├── t_dingtalk.nim\n│   ├── t_discord.nim\n│   ├── t_email.nim                      ← Email adapter tests\n│   ├── t_feishu.nim\n│   ├── t_matrix.nim\n│   ├── t_qq.nim\n│   ├── t_qq_official.nim\n│   ├── t_qq_webhook.nim\n│   ├── t_signal.nim\n│   ├── t_slack.nim\n│   ├── t_telegram.nim\n│   ├── t_wechat.nim\n│   ├── t_wecom\n│   └── t_whatsapp.nim\n├── config/\n│   ├── t_clawhub_registry.nim\n│   ├── t_loader.nim\n│   └── t_skills_registry.nim\n├── core/\n│   ├── t_actor.nim\n│   ├── t_agent_events.nim\n│   ├── t_command_routing.nim\n│   ├── t_debounce.nim\n│   ├── t_diagnostics.nim\n│   ├── t_dns.nim\n│   ├── t_log.nim\n│   ├── t_native_tool_dispatch.nim\n│   ├── t_network.nim\n│   ├── t_onboarding.nim\n│   ├── t_outbound.nim\n│   ├── t_output_sanitizer.nim\n│   ├── t_pipeops.nim                    ← pipeops tests\n│   ├── t_secret_scan.nim\n│   ├── t_session_ingress.nim\n│   ├── t_smart_routing.nim\n│   └── t_tool_loop.nim\n├── domain/\n│   ├── channels/\n│   │   ├── t_dingtalk_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_discord_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_feishu_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_qq_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_signal_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_slack_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_telegram_pure.nim\n│   │   ├── t_wechat_pure.nim\n│   │   └── t_whatsapp_pure.nim\n│   ├── t_builtin_tools.nim\n│   ├── t_calc.nim\n│   ├── t_identity.nim\n│   ├── t_message.nim\n│   ├── t_more_tools.nim\n│   ├── t_personality.nim\n│   └── t_reminder.nim\n├── embedding/\n│   └── t_openrouter_embed.nim\n├── http/\n│   └── t_std_http.nim\n├── ipc/\n│   └── t_ipc_types.nim\n├── memory/\n│   ├── t_contract.nim\n│   ├── t_postgres_memory.nim\n│   └── t_reminder_store.nim\n├── ports/\n│   └── t_channel.nim\n├── provider/\n│   ├── t_anthropic.nim\n│   ├── t_gemini.nim\n│   ├── t_minimax.nim\n│   ├── t_model_catalog.nim\n│   ├── t_ollama.nim\n│   ├── t_openrouter.nim\n│   └── t_zhipu.nim\n├── secrets/\n│   └── t_contract.nim\n├── tool/\n│   ├── t_deno_skill/\n│   └── t_mcp_client.nim\n└── t_version.nim\n```\n</files>\n\n<answer>\n\n## Summary of the Donkey Codebase\n\n### 1. Architecture Overview\n\nThe project follows **hexagonal architecture** (ports & adapters) with clear separation:\n\n- **`src/donkey/core/`** — Pure functional core (`func`), no I/O. Contains `pipeops.nim`, `types.nim`, pure decision logic.\n- **`src/donkey/domain/`** — Domain types and pure channel parsers (`*_pure.nim`). No side effects.\n- **`src/donkey/ports/`** — Port definitions as Nim `concept` types (structural typing). 8 ports: `channel`, `provider`, `tool`, `memory`, `http`, `embedding`, `secrets`, `ipc`.\n- **`src/donkey/adapters/`** — Concrete implementations that absorb external quirks. Organized by: `channel/`, `provider/`, `tool/`, `memory/`, `http/`, `identity/`, `secrets/`, `embedding/`, `ipc/`, `network/`.\n- **`src/donkey/app/`** — Application shell: orchestrator, session manager, agent runners, wiring.\n- **`src/donkey/config/`** — TOML config loading, registries.\n\n### 2. Channel Adapters (12 channels)\n\nAll channel adapters follow the same pattern:\n- **`domain/channels/*_pure.nim`** — Pure parsing functions (`func`), no I/O\n- **`adapters/channel/*.nim`** — Adapter with `send()`, `receive()`, `ack()`, `sendReturnId()`, `editMessage()`\n- **Identity resolution** via `IdentityResolver` (maps channel-specific IDs → internal `UserId` UUIDs)\n\nExisting channels: **Telegram, Discord, WeCom, WeChat, QQ, Feishu, Slack, WhatsApp, Signal, DingTalk, Matrix, Email**\n\n### 3. ChannelPort Definition (`ports/channel.nim`)\n\n```nim\nChannelPort* = concept c, var vc\n  c.send(OutboundMessage) is Result[void, string]\n  vc.receive() is Result[seq[InboundMessage], string]\n  c.ack(string)\n\nOutboundChannelPort* = object\n  send*:         proc(msg: OutboundMessage): Result[void, string]\n  sendReturnId*: proc(msg: OutboundMessage): Result[string, string]\n  editMessage*:  proc(userId: UserId; msgId, text: string): Result[void, string]\n\nOutboundChannelPorts* = object  # holds one OutboundChannelPort per channel\n  telegram*, discord*, wecom*, wechat*, qq*, feishu*, slack*, whatsapp*, signal*, dingtalk*, matrix*, email*\n```\n\n### 4. pipeops.nim — Pipeline Operators\n\nThree operators for functional composition:\n- **`|>`** — Pipe forward: `a |> f` ≡ `f(a)` (pure unary transforms)\n- **`|>->`** — Pipe into last arg: `a |>-> f(x)` ≡ `f(x, a)` (for 2-arg functions)\n- **`>>=`** — Monadic bind: `r >>= f` ≡ `r.andThen(f)` (fallible Result chains)\n\nAlso exports `results` module and utility `splitChunks()` and `nowMs()`.\n\n### 5. Email Implementation\n\nFully implemented with:\n- **`domain/channels/email_pure.nim`** — RFC 2822 parsing (`parseEmail`, `findHeader`, `toInbound`, `hasAttachment`). Pure `func` only.\n- **`adapters/channel/email.nim`** — `EmailAdapter` with IMAP polling (SSL port 993) and SMTP sending (STARTTLS port 587). Implements `ChannelPort` methods. Uses `std/net` directly (no external deps).\n- **`tests/channel/t_email.nim`** — 272 lines of tests covering identity resolution, adapter construction, email parsing, header extraction, SMTP message building.\n\n### 6. Test Patterns\n\nTests use `std/unittest` with `suite`/`test` blocks:\n```nim\nimport std/[os, unittest]\nimport donkey/adapters/channel/email\n\nsuite \"EmailAdapter construction\":\n  test \"imapHost is stored\":\n    let a = newEmailAdapter(\"imap.example.com\", \"smtp.example.com\", ...)\n    check a.imapHost == \"imap.example.com\"\n```\n\nKey patterns:\n- Temp files for identity resolver tests: `getTempDir() / \"donkey_test_ids_em1.tsv\"` with `defer: removeFile(path)`\n- No network calls in unit tests — only construction, pure parsing, and field validation\n- Architecture boundary tests in `tests/architecture/t_boundaries.nim`\n\n### 7. Build Configuration (`donkey.nimble`)\n\n```nim\nversion     = \"0.1.0\"\nsrcDir      = \"src\"\nbin         = @[\"donkey\"]\nrequires \"nim >= 2.0.0\"\nrequires \"chronos >= 4.0.0\"\nrequires \"nimcrypto >= 0.6.0\"\nrequires \"parsetoml >= 0.6.0\"\nrequires \"results >= 0.5.0\"\nrequires \"ws >= 0.5.0\"\nrequires \"db_connector >= 0.1.0\"   # PostgreSQL + pgvector + AGE\nrequires \"illwill >= 0.4.0\"        # TUI dashboard\nrequires \"checksums >= 0.2.0\"      # SHA1 for WeChat webhook\ntask test, \"Run all tests\":\n  exec \"testament --megatest:off all\"\n```\n\n### 8. Core Types (`core/types.nim`)\n\n```nim\nUserId*    = distinct string\nSessionId* = distinct string\nChannelKind* = enum\n  ckTelegram, ckDiscord, ckWeCom, ckWeChat, ckQQ, ckFeishu, ckSlack, ckWhatsApp,\n  ckSignal, ckDingTalk, ckMatrix, ckEmail\n```\n\n### 9. All Port Definitions\n\n| Port | File | Key Methods |\n|------|------|-------------|\n| `ChannelPort` | `ports/channel.nim` | `send`, `receive`, `ack` |\n| `ProviderPort` | `ports/provider.nim` | `complete(CompletionRequest)`, `caps()` |\n| `ToolPort` | `ports/tool.nim` | `listTools()`, `invoke(ToolCall)` |\n| `MemoryPort` | `ports/memory.nim` | `hasProfile`, `loadContext`, `saveUserMd`, `appendMemory`, `savePreferences` |\n| `HttpPort` | `ports/http.nim` | `get`, `post`, `put`, `patch` |\n| `EmbeddingPort` | `ports/embedding.nim` | `embed(string)` |\n| `SecretStore` | `ports/secrets.nim` | `encrypt`, `decrypt`, `isEncrypted`, `enabled`, `label` |\n\n</answer>\n</results>\n</task_result>"
